+## September 27, 2026 — bounded score feature
+
+Added one point for the opposing player on each side-wall exit and two readable
+top-of-screen counters. The wall still calls the ball's existing reset unchanged;
+scoring is an additional signal handled by a separate score node. No movement,
+speed, rebound or reset values changed. License and source attribution remain.
+
+The new headless score route used only the four normal paddle input actions and
+did not write the ball or either score. On Godot 4.7.2 it produced one real contact
+at each wall, a 1–1 score, matching labels, and passed all five checks.
+
+The existing 60 FPS input route was also run unmodified. Nine checks passed, but
+the route recorded no ceiling contact and exited 1; it did record both walls,
+both paddles, the floor, acceleration, and all four paddle bounds. A separate
+supported 30 FPS run also failed (including its bounds) and was not substituted
+for a passing result. These machine failures are reported, not waived, and do
+not claim a human playtest.
